Q: Issues with Laravel Session Configuration - Session Available in Controller but Not in Middleware A: <p>The <code>Session::has('user')</code> is <code>true</code> in your controller but <code>false</code> in the middleware usually pointd to the middleware running before the session has actually been started or outside the web middleware pipline.</p>
<p>Personally, i'd avoid registering <code>StartSession</code> globally unless you really need sessions everywhere. i'dd rather make sure your middleware runs after the web group has initialized the session.</p>
<p>I'd do something like this:</p>
<pre><code>-&gt;withMiddleware(function (Middleware $middleware) {
    $middleware-&gt;alias([
        'checkUser' =&gt; \App\Http\Middleware\CheckUser::class,
    ]);
    $middleware-&gt;appendToGroup('web', \App\Http\Middleware\CheckUser::class);
})
</code></pre>
<p>Then just make sure the routes that need the session are using the web middle group.</p>
<pre><code>Route::middleware(['web', 'checkUser'])-&gt;group(function(){
});
</code></pre>
<p>Another thing i'd probably change is storing the whole Eloquent model in the session (if tha's what <code>$User</code> is). I usually just store something like the user ID and role.</p>
<pre><code>Session::put('user_id', $user-&gt;id);
Session::put('role', $role);
</code></pre>
